        {
          "resource_id": "monster_action",
          "stats": {
            "action_name": {
              "value": "Death Gasp"
            },
            "action_description": {
              "value": "(divine, necromancy)\n\nThe angheuvore draws in a deep breath and holds it, temporarily suspending their biological processes and becoming undead. The angheuvore gains the undead trait and becomes immune to bleed, death effects, disease, paralyzed, poison, and sleep. Any such effects the angheuvore is currently suffering from are suspended, but take effect again once they take a breath."
            },
            "action_type": {
              "value": "none"
            },
            "action_cost": {
              "value": "one_action"
            },
            "action_attack_bonus": {
              "value": 0
            },
            "action_damage_variants": {
              "value": []
            },
            "id": "70e55bb4-f258-4a66-a4be-c287a18f6c9e",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-04-15T14:13:01.886886"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_action",
          "stats": {
            "action_name": {
              "value": "Invigorating Feast"
            },
            "action_description": {
              "value": "(manipulate)\n\nRequirements: The angheuvore is adjacent to a paralyzed, restrained, or unconscious creature, or a deceased creature that died in the last hour\n\nThe angheuvore feasts upon the creature, dealing their jaws Strike damage (basic Fortitude save); a corpse automatically critically fails with no save. If the target takes damage, the angheuvore gains 5 temporary Hit Points and a +10-foot circumstance bonus to their Speeds for 1 minute."
            },
